From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Tue, 18 Apr 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: refresh FFA responses after cost elimination

Activation costs can remove links after QuickEffect's responder was queued.
Choose from the new living top link before issuing that prompt. If no live
link remains, let chain cleanup finish before the one normal open-state
round; do not offer a redundant pre-CHAIN_END round.

R-FFA-CHAIN, owner decision 2026-10-06. Tag and n2 paths stay unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jo347fwscScmug26ujsNN2
---
 processor.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/processor.cpp b/processor.cpp
index 44ec175..01cbb50 100644
--- a/processor.cpp
+++ b/processor.cpp
@@ -1171,6 +1171,22 @@ bool field::process(Processors::QuickEffect& arg) {
 		return FALSE;
 	}
 	case 2: {
+		if(n_duelists > 2 && n_teams == n_duelists
+			&& std::any_of(core.current_chain.begin(), core.current_chain.end(), [](const chain& ch) { return ch.removed_by_elimination; })) {
+			// AddChain can remove links while paying a cost, after this process's
+			// priority was chosen. Refresh it only now, before issuing a prompt.
+			auto* top = get_current_chain();
+			if(!top) {
+				// Let the caller clean up the removed slots and emit CHAIN_END.
+				// Its post-chain PointEvent supplies the single open-state round.
+				core.select_chains.clear();
+				for(uint8_t p = 0; p < n_duelists; ++p)
+					core.hint_timing[p] &= TIMING_DAMAGE_STEP | TIMING_DAMAGE_CAL;
+				return TRUE;
+			}
+			core.response_anchor = top->triggering_player;
+			priority = arg.priority_player = first_responder();
+		}
 		if(n_duelists > 2 && !is_alive(priority)) {
 			// an eliminated duelist is not asked: step 3 takes this as a pass
 			core.select_chains.clear();
